     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. The specialist's recommendation and the chart note are claims I can't verify. Even if both are accurate, 1000 mg/day is five times the labeled maximum of 200 mg/day. I know of no guideline or protocol that supports it. The main risks are serotonin toxicity, seizures, and arrhythmia. Taking it to a specialist and a pharmacist is the safer path than putting it into the system.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** For example, I can enter sertraline 200 mg PO once daily, or any dose up to that maximum.\n- **Support a verification step.** I can help you write a message to the specialist and pharmacy to confirm the dose and document the rationale. A pharmacist can review it and enter it through their own process if it holds up.\n- **Look at other options.** If standard dosing failed, the specialist might consider augmentation, switching agents, or a different class. Those decisions belong to the treating team.\n\nTell me which you'd like. If you want a lower dose entered, give me the dose."
      }
     ],
